## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP on partitioning with a minimax objective, a practical budgeting scenario.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions; - Recurrence: min over j of max of subproblem and block sum; - Reconstruction via parent pointers.

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch
function partitionMinMaxSum(a, k) {
  const n = a.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+a[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=pref[i+1];
  for (let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for (let i=0;i<n;i++){
      for (let j=0;j<i;j++){
        const val = Math.max(dp[j][t-1], pref[i+1]-pref[j+0]);
        if (val<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n-1][Math.min(k,n)], cuts: par};
}
```

